OVERVIEW: Test DICOM connectivity using C-ECHO (verification service)

Performs DICOM C-ECHO verification to test connectivity with PACS servers.
This is the simplest DICOM network operation and is useful for testing
connectivity, network configuration, and PACS server availability.

The host argument accepts a hostname or IP address, optionally with a
port suffix (host:port). Use --port to specify the port separately.
If no port is given, the default is 11112.

Examples:
  dicom-echo server:11112 --aet TEST_SCU
  dicom-echo server --port 11112 --aet TEST_SCU
  dicom-echo server:11112 --aet TEST_SCU --called-aet PACS_SCP
  dicom-echo 192.168.1.100:11112 --aet TEST_SCU --count 10 --stats
  dicom-echo server:11112 --aet TEST_SCU --verbose
  dicom-echo server:11112 --aet TEST_SCU --diagnose

USAGE: dicom-echo <host> [--port <port>] --aet <aet> [--called-aet <called-aet>] [--count <count>] [--timeout <timeout>] [--stats] [--diagnose] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <host>                  PACS server hostname or IP address, optionally with
                          port (host:port)

OPTIONS:
  --port <port>           PACS server port (default: 11112, overrides port in
                          host argument)
  --aet <aet>             Local Application Entity Title (calling AE)
  --called-aet <called-aet>
                          Remote Application Entity Title (default: ANY-SCP)
                          (default: ANY-SCP)
  -c, --count <count>     Number of echo requests to send (default: 1)
                          (default: 1)
  --timeout <timeout>     Connection timeout in seconds (default: 30) (default:
                          30)
  --stats                 Show statistics (min/avg/max round-trip time)
  --diagnose              Run network diagnostics
  -v, --verbose           Show verbose output including connection details
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

